    "job_identity": "006-shortest-war-ever:pilot-character-100:r001",
    "prompt_text": "Create exactly 5.00 seconds of landscape 16:9 animation at 24 fps, composed for 1024×576. <Picture 1> is the sole full-frame scene reference and controls exact setting, figure silhouettes, illustrated surface, object count and placement. Render every pixel as one cohesive detailed hand-inked ChronoStick world: round off-white heads, tiny black dot eyes, spare stick limbs, bold clean dark contours, period-grounded clothing and vessels, muted sand, parchment, teal and navy, soft drawn shadows. The immediate story phase is 27 August 1896 battle end; Khalid reaches consulate before surrender. The visible starting inventory is one Khalid in ivory turban and maroon robe, one neutral consular guard, one consulate gate. Keep the composition medium street-height view, Khalid left approaching the consulate gate right. The camera is one restrained slow push of less than five percent, completed by 4.20s. From 0.00 to 0.80 seconds, establish the reference's existing physical arrangement, steady light, subject count and object condition. From 0.80 to 3.80 seconds, perform exactly this one primary visible action: Khalid reaches the German consulate gate from the palace street and stops at its threshold. Limit background activity to at most a slight cloth, water or smoke movement already present in the reference. From 3.80 to 4.60 seconds, stop the primary action and preserve its resulting positions and damage state. From 4.60 to 5.00 seconds, hold a fully resolved final frame with no new event, jump, duplication or camera movement. No readable letters, digits, labels, dates or captions appear anywhere in this clip. Sound: one stone footstep or wooden gate click, then silence; leave silence between isolated effects. No speech, generated narration, vocal reactions, mouth movement tied to speech, subtitles, lyric text, montage panels, alternate views, extra foreground people, extra ships or photorealistic pixels. NO BACKGROUND MUSIC. Natural diegetic sound effects only.\n\nAUDIO LOCK — SOUND EFFECTS ONLY. Generate only literal, natural, synchronized diegetic sound effects caused by the visible actions and environment.\nNo music. Do not generate music or musical sound design of any kind: no melody, harmony, rhythm bed, beat, percussion, tonal drone, tonal pad, pulse, strings, piano, synth, choir, cinematic score, soundtrack, transition sting, or singing. Do not turn wind, engines, rumbles, ambience, or impacts into tonal or rhythmic music.\nNo dialogue. No narration. No speech. No whispers. No human vocalization. No voices.\nNO BACKGROUND MUSIC. Natural diegetic sound effects only.",
